 "sample": "GREMIO:\nGood morrow, neighbour to my sovereign.\nIn what votion is my fortune,\nAnd, art as by this unfold with me,\nThat a very time should slily by all:\nFor some hours ere I have received,\nComploy the duke's ghost object my kneel, and then his father's liberty,\nWhich so false executioner,\nTo shed and all many a princely daughter,\nShe doth my sweet say to the Tower,\nMore unbalt may descend--\nTo keep it by all grow with wish aged life,\nTwear my good lord. Go's name, villain;",
